+## Continuous Sync control package (development)
+
+The continuous-Sync owner keeps the realtime contract unchanged: no beat-grid work or new synchronization primitive is added to `Engine::process()`. Deterministic owner tests cover rate-only maintenance inside the phase deadband, bounded phase correction without rate churn, oversized phase rejection without transport drift, Beat Loop ownership conflicts, master Slip-Reverse conflicts and invalid correction-envelope parameters.
+
+The native integration toggles follower lock state explicitly, clears stale locks on master/follower clip replacement, services playing decks at 5 Hz from the message thread, suspends maintenance while native Jog/Scratch is active and reports fail-closed lock release for transport/grid/rate-envelope conflicts. Exact-head Linux sanitizer and Windows x64 native build/smoke validation are required before this package can merge. Passing them will still not qualify controller timing, physical latency, arbitrary-music grid accuracy or live use.
+
 ## Audio quality hardening coverage
 
 `brokedj_quality_tests` covers stable playback, pause/seek transitions, loop-wrap continuity, cue switching continuity, control automation, master/cue output protection and cue routing isolation. `brokedj_render_metrics_tests` adds reproducible numeric transition and pitch-changing rate-conversion measurements, including multi-rate high-frequency passband/stopband evidence for downsampling. `brokedj_realtime_contract_tests` adds zero-heap callback coverage plus path-specific diagnostic cost measurements. The optional time-stretch tests separately validate bounded processor/deck/source/device bridge behavior without changing ordinary playback. These tests support implementation hardening; reviewed listening on representative material and devices remains required before stronger sound-quality claims.
